// Tool calls the host application answers, over a socket it opens itself.
//
// A host application frequently cannot be reached from a satellite: it has no
// public address, and nothing between the two was arranged for the satellite to
// dial in. What always works is the direction every other SDK call already
// travels, host to satellite. So the host application opens
// `GET /v1/threads/{id}/relay` as a WebSocket, the satellite sends each tool call
// an agent makes down it as a `SatelliteRelayFrame`, and the host answers up the
// same socket with a `ClientRelayFrame`.
//
// Frames are binary protobuf, one message per WebSocket frame, behind the same
// bearer check as every other authenticated route.
//
// The relay is live only. A call is meaningful while an agent is waiting on it,
// so nothing is persisted and nothing is replayed to a client that attaches
// later: a call made while no client is attached fails at once, as a tool error
// the agent reads.

